  "sunnahDuaEatingSunnahsTitle": "Eating Sunnahs",
  "sunnahDuaEatingSunnahsSubtitle": "The du'a is one part of the whole eating adab",
  "sunnahDuaEatingSunnahsPointsRaw": "Begin with Allah's name before eating.||Eat with the right hand.||Eat from the food nearest to you.||Avoid criticizing food and stop before overfilling yourself.",
  "sunnahDuaEatingSunnahsPractice": "Use the card as a small checklist at meals. Say the du'a, then keep the manners through the whole meal.",
  "sunnahDuaMiswakTitle": "Miswakh",
  "sunnahDuaMiswakSubtitle": "Freshen the mouth before worship",
  "sunnahDuaMiswakPointsRaw": "Use it before wudu or prayer when easy.||Keep the mouth clean before Quran recitation.||Refresh the mouth after waking or before sleep.||Keep the miswakh clean and replace it when worn.",
  "sunnahDuaMiswakArabic": "السِّوَاك",
  "sunnahDuaMiswakPronunciation": "As-siwak",
  "sunnahDuaMiswakTranslation": "Using miswak, or cleaning the teeth when miswak is unavailable, keeps the mouth ready for prayer, wudu, and recitation.",
  "sunnahDuaMiswakPractice": "Keep a miswak near your wudu space or prayer mat so this sunnah becomes an easy daily habit.",
  "sunnahDuaMiswakSource": "Sunnah of purification",
  "sunnahDuaSleepingSunnahsTitle": "Sleeping Sunnahs",
  "sunnahDuaSleepingSunnahsSubtitle": "End the day with remembrance and calm",
  "sunnahDuaSleepingSunnahsPointsRaw": "Make wudu before sleep when you are able.||Dust or check the bed before lying down.||Sleep on the right side.||Close the day with the sleeping du'a and remembrance.",
  "sunnahDuaSleepingSunnahsPractice": "Keep the sleep routine short and repeatable so it survives tired nights too.",
  "sunnahDuaHomeSunnahsTitle": "Home Sunnahs",
  "sunnahDuaHomeSunnahsSubtitle": "Enter and leave with salam, remembrance, and trust",
  "sunnahDuaHomeSunnahsPointsRaw": "Say bismillah when entering.||Give salam to the people at home.||Leave home with trust in Allah.||Make the first and last moments at home peaceful.",
  "sunnahDuaHomeSunnahsPractice": "Attach this routine to the doorway so the habit triggers naturally.",
  "sunnahDuaWuduSunnahsTitle": "Wudu Sunnahs",
  "sunnahDuaWuduSunnahsSubtitle": "Purification with mindful details",
  "sunnahDuaWuduSunnahsPointsRaw": "Begin with Allah's name.||Wash carefully without wasting water.||Give each limb its due attention.||Finish with the testimony after wudu.",
  "sunnahDuaWuduSunnahsPractice": "Slow down enough that wudu feels like preparation for salah, not just a task.",
  "sunnahDuaSiyamSunnahsTitle": "Siyam",
  "sunnahDuaSiyamSunnahsSubtitle": "Sunnah fasting beyond Ramadan",
  "sunnahDuaSiyamSunnahsPointsRaw": "Keep the intention sincere and clear before the fast.||Guard the fast beyond food and drink: protect speech, anger, eyes, and actions.||Fast Mondays and Thursdays when you are able.||Keep three days each lunar month, especially Ayyam al-Bid: the 13th, 14th, and 15th.||Remember special sunnah fasts: six days of Shawwal, Ashura, and the day of Arafah for those not at Hajj.||Take suhur close to Fajr and hasten iftar after sunset.||Break the fast with dates or water and make du'a at iftar.||Do not harm yourself; leave voluntary fasts when sick, travelling, or when duties would be neglected.",
  "sunnahDuaSiyamArabic": "الصِّيَامُ جُنَّةٌ",
  "sunnahDuaSiyamPronunciation": "As-siyamu junnah",
  "sunnahDuaSiyamTranslation": "Fasting is a shield.",
  "sunnahDuaSiyamSunnahsPractice": "Start with one sustainable sunnah fast, then build slowly. The goal is not just hunger; it is taqwa, restraint, gratitude, and a cleaner heart before Allah.",
  "sunnahDuaSiyamSource": "Sahih al-Bukhari 1894; Sahih Muslim 1151, 1162, 1164; Jami' at-Tirmidhi 761",
  "sunnahDuaMasjidSunnahsTitle": "Masjid Sunnahs",
  "sunnahDuaMasjidSunnahsSubtitle": "Enter the masjid with mercy and composure",
  "sunnahDuaMasjidSunnahsPointsRaw": "Enter calmly and avoid rushing.||Ask Allah to open the doors of mercy.||Keep the phone and talk quiet.||Leave with gratitude and ask Allah from His bounty.",
  "sunnahDuaMasjidSunnahsPractice": "Let the masjid doorway become a reminder to lower noise, hurry, and distraction.",
  "sunnahDuaSneezingSunnahTitle": "Sneezing Sunnah",
  "sunnahDuaSneezingSunnahSubtitle": "A tiny moment of gratitude and mercy",
  "sunnahDuaSneezingSunnahPointsRaw": "Say alhamdulillah after sneezing.||A listener responds with mercy.||The sneezer replies with guidance and goodness.||Keep the exchange gentle and brief.",
  "sunnahDuaSneezingSunnahPractice": "This is small, but it turns an ordinary moment into gratitude and care.",
  "sunnahDuaSeekingForgivenessSubtitle": "Keep istighfar close",
  "sunnahDuaSeekingForgivenessPractice": "Repeat it between tasks, after salah, or whenever the heart feels heavy.",
  "sunnahDuaDifficultySubtitle": "When the heart feels crowded",
  "sunnahDuaDifficultyPractice": "Read it slowly, then choose the next right action with trust in Allah.",
